/* Symbols the rakupp EXECUTABLE must carry in its dynamic symbol table, so a
 * dlopen'ed extension can resolve them (see docs/guide/EXTENSIONS.md).
 *
 * ELF only. Without this, an extension's first rk_* call dies with an
 * "undefined symbol" error: a plain ELF executable keeps its symbols out of
 * .dynsym, unlike Mach-O (exports by default) and Windows (RK_API's dllexport
 * plus the import library). The alternative, -rdynamic, would export every
 * C++ symbol in the interpreter — thousands of accidental ABI promises and a
 * fatter binary for nothing.
 *
 * The glob means a new rk_* entry point is picked up without touching this
 * file. Understood by GNU ld, gold and lld.
 */
{ rk_*; };
